title: System Tree
manual:

The tree lists the loaded systems, one row each, and is where the current system is
chosen: the main view, the input console and the tool windows follow it. A file with
several geometries (SCF or optimization steps) comes in as a group under a header row.

# Columns

- The first columns hold the close button, the expand triangle of a group, the "Id", an
  icon for the "File format" and the "System properties" icons: scalar fields loaded
  (click it to show or hide the field list), vibration data, partial site occupancies
  (disorder) and critical points.
- "Name" shows the name of the system. Right-click the header for the hidden columns
  ("Symmetry", "Volume/Å³", numbers of atoms, Z, Z', cell parameters, energy,
  pressure). Clicking a header sorts by it.

# Header row

- The "❇" button opens the tree menu: "Expand All", "Collapse All", "Plot Tree Data...",
  "Save Multiple...", "Close Selected", "Close Visible" and "Close All".
- The filter box keeps the rows whose name matches it: comma-separated fields are
  alternatives and a leading - excludes (inc1,inc2,-exc). "Clear" empties it. The
  numbers of shown and selected systems follow the box.

# Selection

A click makes a row the current system and selects it alone; control-click toggles single
rows and shift-click selects a range. "All", "None" and "Toggle" select every
visible system, deselect all but the current one, or invert the selection. "Close
Selected", the Delete key and the "All" button of the view act on the selection. The
preferences "Tree selects view system" and "Tree selects input console system" decide
whether the main view and the input console follow the tree; J and K move to the next
and the previous system.

# Fields

The triangle before the name, or a double-click on the row, opens the list of the fields
of the system; the reference field is outlined. Click a field to make it the reference,
and right-click it for its menu (rename, duplicate, evaluation options, "Critical
Points...", "New Isosurface", "Remove"). The red X of a field removes it; the Delete key
removes the reference field while the list is open and closes the selected systems
otherwise.

# Context menu

Right-click a system for "Set as Current System", "Rename", "Duplicate", "Display in New
View", "View/Edit Geometry...", "Describe in Output Window", the "Fields", "Vibrations"
and "Critical Points" submenus, "Save Scene...", "Restore from File" and "Close".
